{#
   The search box.

   `GET`, so a search is an address a reader can bookmark, share and go back to —
   which is what a search result should be, and what a POST would take away.

   The query is redisplayed as typed. Twig escapes it, so a query made of markup
   appears as the characters somebody typed rather than as markup; FR-011 is
   about a reader being able to see and correct what they asked for, and it is
   also the reason a search box is a classic place to find an injection.

   **One control, not two side by side.** The input and the button share an
   outline, a height and a corner radius, and the focus ring is drawn around the
   pair by `focus-within` — so tabbing to either lights the whole thing rather
   than half of it. Before feature 018 these were two elements with a gap and
   different radii, which read as two things that happened to be adjacent.

   **Everything the suggestion list needs is here, and none of it does anything
   without JavaScript.** `role="combobox"` and its attributes describe a control
   whose list is empty until a script fills it; a browser with no script finds a
   search form that submits, which is exactly what it found before. The list
   element is written by `assets/suggestions.js` rather than sitting here empty,
   so a reader is never told about a listbox that will not arrive.

   Parameters: `query` (what to redisplay), `autofocus`, `size` — 'large' on the
   search page, anything else in the header. No margin of its own: spacing is the
   caller's business, and a component that carries `mt-6` cannot sit on a header
   line without pushing it down.
#}
{% set large = size|default('') == 'large' %}

{# `relative` so the suggestion list can be positioned against this form. It is
   here rather than added by the script, because a script that has to lay the
   page out is a script whose absence changes the layout. #}
<form method="get"
      action="{{ path('search') }}"
      role="search"
      class="relative"
      data-search-suggest
      data-search-suggest-url="{{ path('search_suggestions') }}"
      data-search-suggest-minimum="{{ constant('App\\Search\\SearchQuery::MINIMUM_LENGTH') }}">
    <label for="{{ id|default('site-search') }}" class="sr-only">Search</label>

    <div class="flex items-stretch overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-rule bg-white
                focus-within:border-accent focus-within:ring-2 focus-within:ring-accent/25">
        {#
           `type="search"` rather than `text`: it gives a clear control in the
           browsers that draw one, and Escape empties the field — which is why
           the script below closes its list on Escape without also clearing.
        #}
        <input type="search"
               id="{{ id|default('site-search') }}"
               name="q"
               value="{{ query|default('') }}"
               placeholder="Search"
               maxlength="{{ constant('App\\Search\\SearchQuery::MAXIMUM_LENGTH') }}"
               autocomplete="off"
               role="combobox"
               aria-expanded="false"
               aria-autocomplete="list"
               {% if autofocus|default(false) %}autofocus{% endif %}
               data-search-suggest-input
               class="w-full min-w-0 border-0 bg-transparent text-ink outline-none placeholder:text-muted
                      {{ large ? 'px-4 py-3 text-base' : 'px-3 py-2 text-sm' }}">

        <button type="submit"
                class="shrink-0 border-l border-rule font-medium text-muted transition-colors
                       hover:bg-ink hover:text-white focus:bg-ink focus:text-white focus:outline-none
                       {{ large ? 'px-5 text-base' : 'px-4 text-sm' }}">
            Search
        </button>
    </div>
</form>
